// Track MI (docs/roadmap/llvm-roadmap.md), MI29: stack probes. `big` has
// a value for each of its many operations, so its frame on the machine
// layer (compiler/nat_ir.fd, one slot per IR value) spans several pages;
// the prologue then moves sp one page at a time and touches each page
// (ng_probe_frame: unrolled up to two pages, a counted loop past that), so
// a large frame cannot step over a stack's guard page. `mid` has a frame
// of about two pages (the unrolled probes), and `both` puts one large
// frame below another. FID_NAT_OFF=probe: one subtraction, as before.
// Native check: NATIVE=1 bash scripts/cross-test.sh aarch64-linux
// (and riscv64-linux, x86_64-linux, x86_64-windows).
// Generated: each line of `big` is v<n> = x * (n + 1) + n, of `mid`
// w<n> = x * (n + 3) - n, each summed.
// Expected output:
// 360000
// 540300
// 720600
// 540
// 67140
// 377190

